### ─── BASIC READS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §4. Get a single laptop by key
### Returns the document directly (no array wrapper) for single-key lookups.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp2"
}

### §5. Get all laptops (returns JSON array with _key in each element)
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops"
}

### §6. Get a batch of specific laptops by key array
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": ["lp1", "lp3", "lp5"]
}

### ─── FIELD SELECTION (GraphQL-style) ────────────────────────────────────────

### §7. Select only brand, model and price — nothing else sent over the wire
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"]
}

### §8. Deep nested field selection — only the CPU clock speed buried 3 levels deep
### Response: [ { "_key": "lp1", "specs": { "cpu": { "ghz": 3.5 } } }, ... ]
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.cpu.ghz", "specs.cpu.cores"]
}

### §9. excludedFields — return everything except price and the foreign key IDs
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "excludedFields": ["price", "memory_id", "display_id"]
}

### §10. Validation error — fields and excludedFields cannot be used together
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand"],
  "excludedFields": ["price"]
}

### ─── WHERE CLAUSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §11. Exact equality — only Apple laptops
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": { "brand": "Apple" }
}

### §12. Numeric range — laptops priced between 1000 and 2000
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": {
    "price": { "$gt": 1000, "$lt": 2000 }
  }
}

### §13. Nested field WHERE — laptops with 12+ CPU cores
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.cpu"],
  "where": {
    "specs.cpu.cores": { "$gte": 12 }
  }
}

### §14. Multiple conditions (implicit AND) — Intel laptops under 2kg
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.cpu.brand", "specs.weight_kg"],
  "where": {
    "specs.cpu.brand": "Intel",
    "specs.weight_kg": { "$lt": 2.0 }
  }
}

### §15. $ne — all laptops NOT made by Intel
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.cpu.brand"],
  "where": {
    "specs.cpu.brand": { "$ne": "Intel" }
  }
}

### §16. $contains on a string field — models containing "Pro"
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model"],
  "where": {
    "model": { "$contains": "Pro" }
  }
}

### §17. $contains on an array field — laptops tagged as "gaming"
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "tags", "price"],
  "where": {
    "tags": { "$contains": "gaming" }
  }
}

### §18. $in — laptops from a specific brand shortlist
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": {
    "brand": { "$in": ["Apple", "Dell", "Razer"] }
  }
}

### §19. $nin — exclude budget/modular brands
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": {
    "brand": { "$nin": ["Framework"] }
  }
}

### §20. Combined WHERE — in-stock gaming laptops under $2000
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price", "tags"],
  "where": {
    "in_stock": true,
    "tags": { "$contains": "gaming" },
    "price": { "$lt": 2000 }
  }
}

### ─── SORT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §21. Sort by price ascending — cheapest first
### Expected: Framework(849), Lenovo(1499), Asus(1699), Dell(1899), Razer(2499), Apple(3499)
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "sort": [{ "field": "price", "order": "asc" }]
}

### §22. Sort by price descending — most expensive first
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "sort": [{ "field": "price", "order": "desc" }]
}

### §23. Sort by nested field — most CPU cores first
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.cpu.cores", "specs.cpu.ghz"],
  "sort": [{ "field": "specs.cpu.cores", "order": "desc" }]
}

### §24. Multi-field sort — brand asc, then price asc within same brand
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "sort": [
    { "field": "brand", "order": "asc" },
    { "field": "price", "order": "asc" }
  ]
}

### §25. Sort + WHERE — in-stock laptops sorted by weight (lightest first)
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "specs.weight_kg", "price"],
  "where": { "in_stock": true },
  "sort": [{ "field": "specs.weight_kg", "order": "asc" }]
}

### ─── PAGINATION (count + offset) ───────────────────────────────────────────

### §26. count — return only the 3 cheapest laptops
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "sort": [{ "field": "price", "order": "asc" }],
  "count": 3
}

### §27. offset + count — page 2 of laptops sorted by price (skip 2, take 2)
### Expected: Asus(1699), Dell(1899)
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "sort": [{ "field": "price", "order": "asc" }],
  "offset": 2,
  "count": 2
}

### §28. offset + count + WHERE — page 2 of in-stock laptops by price
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": { "in_stock": true },
  "sort": [{ "field": "price", "order": "asc" }],
  "offset": 2,
  "count": 2
}

### ─── JOINS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §29. Join laptops → memory — embed full memory spec for each laptop
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "ram": { "from": "memory", "on": "memory_id" } }
  ]
}

### §30. Join laptops → display — embed only refresh_hz and panel type
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model"],
  "joins": [
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["refresh_hz", "panel", "size_inch"] } }
  ]
}

### §31. Double join — embed both memory and display in one query
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "ram":    { "from": "memory",  "on": "memory_id",  "fields": ["capacity_gb", "type"] } },
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["size_inch", "refresh_hz", "panel"] } }
  ]
}

### §32. Join + WHERE on main collection — only in-stock laptops with their display info
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": { "in_stock": true },
  "joins": [
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["refresh_hz", "panel", "hdr"] } }
  ]
}

### §33. Join + WHERE on joined field — laptops with an OLED or Mini-LED display
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["panel", "refresh_hz", "hdr"] } }
  ],
  "where": {
    "screen.panel": { "$in": ["OLED", "Mini-LED"] }
  }
}

### §34. Join + WHERE on joined field — laptops with 120Hz+ display
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["refresh_hz", "panel"] } }
  ],
  "where": {
    "screen.refresh_hz": { "$gte": 120 }
  }
}

### §35. Join + WHERE on joined field — laptops with upgradeable RAM
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "ram": { "from": "memory", "on": "memory_id", "fields": ["capacity_gb", "type", "upgradeable"] } }
  ],
  "where": {
    "ram.upgradeable": true
  }
}

### §36. Join + sort — all laptops sorted by display refresh rate descending
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "joins": [
    { "screen": { "from": "display", "on": "display_id", "fields": ["refresh_hz", "panel"] } }
  ],
  "sort": [{ "field": "screen.refresh_hz", "order": "desc" }]
}

### ─── UPDATE & DELETE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §37. Update a single laptop — mark Dell XPS 15 back in stock and drop price
POST http://localhost:1538/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp2": { "in_stock": true, "price": 3456 }
  }
}

### §38. Update multiple laptops in one call
POST http://localhost:1538/update
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp1": { "price": 1399 },
    "lp6": { "price": 799 }
  }
}

### §39. Delete a single laptop by key
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp6"
}

### §40. Delete multiple laptops in one call
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": ["lp4", "lp5"]
}

### §41. Drop an entire collection
POST http://localhost:1538/delete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "drop": true
}

### ─── RESTFUL GET ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §42. GET single laptop via REST endpoint
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### §43. GET all laptops via REST (paginated — first 3)
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops?limit=3&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### §44. GET all laptops via REST (paginated — next 3)
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops?limit=3&offset=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ─── VERSIONING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §45. Read lp2 — note the _v, createdAt, modifiedAt fields added by the engine
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp2"
}

### §46. Conflict test — send _v:1 when server already has _v:2 → write is skipped
### Run §39 first (which bumps lp4 to _v:2), then run this — it should be ignored.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp4": { "brand": "Dell", "model": "XPS 15 STALE", "price": 999, "_v": 1 }
  }
}

### ─── EXTENDS (inline reference embedding at insert time) ────────────────────
### The "extend" key embeds data from another collection directly into the
### stored document at insert time. The referenced document is fetched once
### and stored as a snapshot — no join needed on reads.
### Format: "extend": { "<alias>": "<collection>.<key>", ... }
### The "extend" key is removed from the final stored document.

### §50. Insert lp7 with embedded memory and display via extend
### ram  → fetches mem4 from the memory collection and embeds it
### screen → fetches dsp3 from the display collection and embeds it
### After this insert, lp7 contains the full mem4 and dsp3 documents inline.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp7": {
      "brand": "MSI",
      "model": "Titan GT77",
      "price": 3299,
      "in_stock": true,
      "tags": ["gaming", "desktop-replacement", "windows"],
      "specs": {
        "cpu": { "brand": "Intel", "cores": 16, "ghz": 5.0 },
        "battery_wh": 99,
        "weight_kg": 3.3
      },
      "extends": {
        "ram":    "memory.mem4",
        "screen": "display.dsp3"
      }
    }
  }
}

### §51. Read lp7 back — ram and screen are now full embedded documents, not pointers
### Expected: ram = { capacity_gb: 64, type: "DDR5", ... }, screen = { size_inch: 15.6, ... }
### The "extend" key is gone — it was consumed at insert time.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp7"
}

### §52. extends with auto-generated key (array format)
### The extend block works identically when data is an array (UUIDv7 keys auto-assigned).
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": [
    {
      "brand": "HP",
      "model": "Spectre x360",
      "price": 1599,
      "in_stock": true,
      "extends": {
        "ram": "memory.mem2"
      }
    }
  ]
}

### §53. extends with a missing reference — insert still succeeds, alias simply not added
### "memory.mem99" does not exist — the insert completes without error,
### and the stored document will have brand/model/price but no "ram" field.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp8": {
      "brand": "Lenovo",
      "model": "Legion 5",
      "price": 1199,
      "extend": {
        "ram": "memory.mem99"
      }
    }
  }
}

### ─── SECURITY / VALIDATION ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §54. Unauthorized access — should return 401
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "collection": "laptops"
}

### §55. Invalid collection name (path traversal attempt) — should return validation error
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "../etc/passwd",
  "data": { "test": { "value": "hack" } }
}

### §56. Reserved collection name — should return validation error
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "admin",
  "data": { "test": { "value": "data" } }
}

### §57. Invalid property set
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "wrongProperty": "test",
  "data": {
    "lp9": {
      "brand": "Lenovo",
      "model": "Legion 5",
      "price": 1199,
      "extend": {
        "ram": "memory.mem99"
      }
    }
  }
}

### §57. Invalid property get
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "myInvalidProperty": "test value",
  "keys": "lp7"
}

### ─── LOGICAL OPERATORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §58. $or — laptops where brand contains "Apple" OR model contains "XPS"
### Expected: Apple MacBook Pro + Dell XPS 15
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model"],
  "where": {
    "$or": [
      { "brand": { "$ct": "Apple" } },
      { "model": { "$ct": "XPS" } }
    ]
  }
}

### §59. $and — laptops that are in stock AND price under $2000
### Expected: same as implicit AND, but using explicit $and syntax
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": {
    "$and": [
      { "in_stock": true },
      { "price": { "$lt": 2000 } }
    ]
  }
}

### §60. $or combined with top-level condition — in-stock laptops from Apple or Dell
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"],
  "where": {
    "in_stock": true,
    "$or": [
      { "brand": { "$eq": "Apple" } },
      { "brand": { "$eq": "Dell" } }
    ]
  }
}

### ─── SCHEMAS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §61. Register a schema for the 'memory' collection
POST http://localhost:1538/schema
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "memory",
  "schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "capacity_gb": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
      "type": { "type": "string" },
      "speed_mhz": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
      "upgradeable": { "type": "boolean" }
    },
    "required": ["capacity_gb", "type", "speed_mhz", "upgradeable"]
  }
}

### §62. Register a schema for the 'display' collection
POST http://localhost:1538/schema
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "display",
  "schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "size_inch": { "type": "number", "minimum": 5 },
      "resolution": { "type": "string" },
      "panel": { "type": "string" },
      "refresh_hz": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 24 },
      "touchscreen": { "type": "boolean" },
      "hdr": { "type": "boolean" }
    },
    "required": ["size_inch", "resolution", "panel", "refresh_hz"]
  }
}

### §63. Register a schema for the 'laptops' collection
POST http://localhost:1538/schema
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "brand": { "type": "string" },
      "model": { "type": "string" },
      "price": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0 },
      "in_stock": { "type": "boolean" },
      "memory_id": { "type": "string" },
      "display_id": { "type": "string" },
      "tags": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "specs": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "cpu": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "brand": { "type": "string" },
              "cores": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
              "ghz": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0.1 }
            }
          },
          "battery_wh": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
          "weight_kg": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0.1 }
        }
      }
    },
    "required": ["brand", "model", "price", "in_stock"]
  }
}

### §64. Test Schema Validation (Failure)
### This will fail because 'price' is missing (required) and 'brand' is not a string.
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "fail1": {
      "brand": 123,
      "model": "Broken Laptop",
      "in_stock": true
    }
  }
}

### ─── RECOVERY & MAINTENANCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### §65. Take a manual snapshot (requires auth)
### This triggers a compaction and creates a new .snapshot.bin file.
### Old snapshots are moved to the /backup folder.
### Requires: *:*:* scope. Collection-level or document-level tokens → 403.
POST http://localhost:1538/snapshot
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ─── AUTHORIZATION & SCOPED TOKENS ──────────────────────────────────────────
###
### MoltenDB uses a single root user. The root user delegates narrow-permission
### JWTs to clients via POST /auth/delegate. Clients never see the root password.
###
### Scope format:  action:collection:document_key
###   action       →  read | write | delete
###   collection   →  exact name, or * for any collection
###   document_key →  exact key
###                   * for any document in the collection
###                   prefix* for any key starting with prefix (e.g. store_A_*)
###   *:*:*        →  special scope granting full access to everything
###
### SCOPE → ENDPOINT COMPATIBILITY
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  Scope                        │ /get │ /collections/:c/docs/:k │ /set │ /update │ /delete │ /snapshot
###  ─────────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────┼─────────┼──────────
###  read:laptops:lp1             │ lp1  │ ✅ lp1 only              │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:lp1,lp2         │lp1+2 │ ✅ lp1 or lp2           │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:store_A_*       │store_A_*│ ✅ store_A_* keys only │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:*               │  ✅  │ ✅ any key               │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  write:laptops:*              │  ❌  │ ❌                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  delete:laptops:*             │  ❌  │ ❌                       │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ✅    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:* + write:*     │  ✅  │ ✅                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:*:* + write:*:*         │  ✅  │ ✅ any col/key           │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  *:*:*                        │  ✅  │ ✅                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ✅    │    ✅
###
### HOW TO USE THESE EXAMPLES
###   1. Make sure you have a valid root token in @token (see §1 at the top).
###   2. Run a "Mint" request below to get a scoped token.
###   3. Copy the returned token value into the matching @variable.
###   4. Run the usage examples with that variable.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LEVEL 1 — DOCUMENT-LEVEL READ (narrowest possible access)
### Scopes: read:laptops:lp1, read:laptops:lp2
###
### This token can only read two specific documents. It cannot query the
### collection, write, delete, or access any other document.
### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Mint — document-level read token
POST http://localhost:1538/auth/delegate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "client_id": "field-rep",
  "scopes": ["read:laptops:lp1", "read:laptops:lp2"],
  "ttl_secs": 3600
}

